      },
      "lineNbr": 194,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-04T21:35:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not clear to me from [the docs](https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/refs/heads/master/include/openssl/ec_key.h#175) whether this does a check to make sure `x` and `y` are actually a point on the curve.\n\nDo we need to call `EC_KEY_check_key`/`EC_KEY_check_fips` or does this function do the validation?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 194,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 194,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "9868ac46032a5be51aa2bd2c4013909fedcbcca2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76857403_43956b54",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor_auth_commands.cc",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 194,
      "author": {
        "id": 1293547
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T12:30:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EC_KEY_set_public_key_affine_coordinates will check if the key is valid or not.\nWe don\u0027t need to do that again.",
      "parentUuid": "dfbac41a_39c734c3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 194,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 194,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "9868ac46032a5be51aa2bd2c4013909fedcbcca2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
